research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34058-fs-homotopy-equivalent-spaces-are-homeomorphic L2 A homeomorphism is in particular a bijection ([[def-homeomorphism-and-open-maps]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34059-ex-a-point-and-r-are-homotopy-equivalent-not-homeomorphic L3 A homeomorphism is a bijection, and $\mathbb R$ is uncountable ([[def-homeomorphism-and-open-maps]], [[thm-r-uncountable]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34060-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34061-### def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34062-lem-homotopy-reflexive-and-symmetric A1 A homotopy rel $A$ is a continuous $K:X\times I\to Y$ with $K(x,0)$ and $K(x,1)$ the prescribed endpoint maps and $K(a,t)$ equal to their common value for every $a\in A$ and $t\in I$ ([[def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34063-lem-homotopy-transitivity-by-reparametrisation A1 The endpoint and relative conditions for $F$ and $G$ are those of [[def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy]].
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34064-thm-composition-respects-homotopy A1 The endpoint and relative conditions are those of [[def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy]].
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34065-thm-two-maps-into-a-convex-set-are-homotopic A1 A homotopy from $f$ to $g$ is a continuous $H:X\times I\to C$ with $H(x,0)=f(x)$ and $H(x,1)=g(x)$ ([[def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log:34066:ex-path-homotopy-through-straight-segments-in-a-convex-set A1 A path homotopy relative endpoints is a homotopy $H:I\times I\to C$ with the path parameter on the first coordinate and with $H(0,t)$ and $H(1,t)$ fixed ([[def-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34067-
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34068-### def-interval
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34069-fs-a-function-with-closed-graph-is-continuous A1 A set $U \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ is open in the usual topology exactly when for every $x \in U$ there is a real $r > 0$ with $(x - r, x + r) \subseteq U$; in particular every bounded open interval is open ([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]], claims 2 and 3, [[def-metrizable-space]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34070-fs-two-continuous-maps-agreeing-on-a-dense-subset-are-equal A1 $U \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ is open in the usual topology exactly when for every $x \in U$ there is a real $r > 0$ with $(x-r, x+r) \subseteq U$ ([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]], claims 2 and 3, [[def-metrizable-space]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34071-ex-the-diagonal-of-the-real-line-is-closed A1 Every bounded open interval is open in $\mathbb{R}$ ([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]], claims 2 and 3, [[def-metrizable-space]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34072-ex-two-continuous-real-functions-agreeing-on-the-rationals-are-equal A1 $U \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ is open in the usual topology exactly when for every $x \in U$ there is a real $r > 0$ with $(x - r, x + r) \subseteq U$ ([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]], claims 2 and 3, [[def-metrizable-space]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34073-cex-two-maps-into-an-indiscrete-space-agreeing-on-a-dense-set A1 $U \subseteq \mathbb{R}$ is open in the usual topology exactly when for every $x \in U$ there is a real $r > 0$ with $(x - r, x + r) \subseteq U$ ([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]], claims 2 and 3, [[def-metrizable-space]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-34074-ex-intervals-and-euclidean-spaces-are-contractible A1 Intervals are order-convex: if $x,c\in J$ and $x\le z\le c$, or $c\le z\le x$, then $z\in J$ ([[def-interval]]).
