research/audit/wave3-impact-audit.json-6712-   "notes": "Descends from 2 materially changed root(s): rem-real-exponents-deferred, thm-holder-finite. rem-real-exponents-deferred — Root change: a stale corpus claim was replaced with an accurate pointer, and the clause naming thm-rational-supremum-power-agrees-with-exp was removed after Alpha established that theorem is false for bases 0 < a < 1 (see wave3-alpha.md A6-F5). This is a rem- item: it proves nothing and is a deps target for orientation only, so no consumer draws a mathematical inference from it. def-real-power and thm-real-power-laws are in forward_refs only, never in deps, so no logical dependence on later material was created. || thm-holder-finite — Root change: the last sentence of Fact [L5] was corrected from \"rational EXPONENTS are read in R through the embedding of Q\" to the accurate split between the rational coefficients 1/p, 1/q (which do pass through lem-of-q-embeds) and the rational exponents p, q (which stay in Q and act through def-rational-power, already a declared dependency). The Statement of Hoelder’s inequality and every numbered step are unchanged. Every one of those changes is a Remark/prose correction, a deletion of a Fact no numbered step cited, a citation made exact, a title corrected to agree with its own Statement, or a dependency added to license a step already taken. None narrowed or strengthened a Statement that a consumer cites, so this consumer remains licensed exactly as before; each root was additionally certified on its current text by an independent GPT 5.6 Sol reader (wave3-alpha.md sections 3.2 and 3.3)."
